              "text": "These interventions created hybrid frameworks that attempted to balance Islamic inheritance principles with the reality of a community in which matrilineal ties remained culturally binding even where they had lost legal force. The Chief Kadhi's rulings acknowledged what the community already knew: that the Digo could not simply choose one system and abandon the other. The matrilineal tradition was too deeply embedded in identity to be overridden by decree, and Islamic law was too central to faith to be ignored."
