              "text": "Islam is the dominant religion on both sides of the border. Mosque communities serve as anchor points for Digo identity in both countries, and religious occasions — Eid al-Fitr, Eid al-Adha, Maulidi — are celebrated with the same fervour and many of the same local customs. Friday prayers draw congregations that include families with members on both sides of the frontier. Religious networks have been, in some ways, more effective than any political institution at maintaining cross-border Digo solidarity."
